523
00:46:31,787 --> 00:46:32,708
[SPEAKER_00]: Precisely what you said.

524
00:46:32,768 --> 00:46:37,310
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, you see yourself... That is the only way that you would develop these things.

525
00:46:37,370 --> 00:46:46,815
[SPEAKER_00]: It's like, you see your defilements, you notice them, you abandon them, you're able to move on to the next aspect.

526
00:46:46,935 --> 00:46:53,219
[SPEAKER_00]: You cannot develop it through, like, doing something else that completely overlooks the place where the pressures are.

527
00:46:53,659 --> 00:46:58,382
[SPEAKER_00]: It has to be developed through abandoning the five hindrances.

528
00:46:59,225 --> 00:47:01,787
[SPEAKER_00]: That is the only way that you can achieve any of these states.

529
00:47:01,807 --> 00:47:07,490
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's why it's not a huge jump when these people were thinking that they were arahants.

530
00:47:07,670 --> 00:47:19,618
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not that they were like super far off the mark and they were just kind of... almost like a cartoonish, conceited, just blind nonsense.

531
00:47:19,698 --> 00:47:27,343
[SPEAKER_00]: No, it was like they have actually been working on that right level of noticing greed, aversion and delusion

532
00:47:27,923 --> 00:47:31,304
[SPEAKER_00]: You're not acting out of it until it actually goes away.

533
00:47:32,525 --> 00:47:39,167
[SPEAKER_00]: And the result of that is the mind ascending into these more subtle and subtle planes.

534
00:47:40,087 --> 00:47:48,271
[SPEAKER_00]: So, yes, with the right view, you have to develop these things, but it would come from a completely different place.

535
00:47:48,951 --> 00:47:57,454
[SPEAKER_00]: You wouldn't be able to develop any kind of... how would you call it, like...

536
00:47:58,392 --> 00:48:15,644
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, losing perspective, making something special out of them, becoming kind of dependent on them, overlooking that, well, no matter how lofty and no matter how even

537
00:48:17,638 --> 00:48:26,142
[SPEAKER_00]: Those planes are more... you could even say they're more fundamental than the other stuff, the normal state of being that you live in.

538
00:48:26,702 --> 00:48:35,406
[SPEAKER_00]: Even then, you wouldn't be able to become dependent on those and overlook that, wait a second, it doesn't matter in which of these my mind is.

539
00:48:36,906 --> 00:48:38,887
[SPEAKER_00]: That is not what the point of this whole training is.

540
00:48:39,027 --> 00:48:46,230
[SPEAKER_00]: The point is that other perpendicular dimension of like, what is my attitude in regard to this?

541
00:48:48,528 --> 00:48:56,032
[SPEAKER_00]: So, in a way, it's the same... it's the same thing that you would have used to develop samādhi.

542
00:48:56,512 --> 00:49:01,254
[SPEAKER_00]: It's like asking yourself where your motivations are and all that stuff.

543
00:49:01,514 --> 00:49:08,737
[SPEAKER_00]: But then, you know, whether you apply it then to the result of that practice or not, that's a different question.

544
00:49:08,797 --> 00:49:09,558
[SPEAKER_00]: And most people don't.

545
00:49:10,198 --> 00:49:12,399
[SPEAKER_00]: Because it feels... without a Buddha, you wouldn't.

546
00:49:12,659 --> 00:49:13,620
[SPEAKER_00]: Because it feels like

547
00:49:14,623 --> 00:49:15,084
[SPEAKER_00]: This is it.

548
00:49:15,384 --> 00:49:19,668
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, it's been purified from everything.

549
00:49:19,808 --> 00:49:27,155
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, only from the outside, somebody from the outside tells you like, wait, no, this is not quite it.

550
00:49:27,215 --> 00:49:34,722
[SPEAKER_00]: Because when you're talking about it, and you're saying, oh, you're additive in regard to it, it sounds like this obvious thing, like, that only a fool would overlook.

551
00:49:35,523 --> 00:49:35,823
[SPEAKER_00]: But no.

